{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788214044,"nonce":"/kfXu0Kya14L+1Zwo5HTM74p0N0=","message":"FROM 4.1 (96d9315, commit b3d79a0) — the playbook contract this spec depends\non is authored. What the loop consumes:\n\n1. Session start: playbook/SESSION-START.md is the ordered load list, files\n   then reads, with named positions (INDEX -\u003e turn.md -\u003e triggered.md -\u003e\n   daily.md -\u003e templates/INDEX -\u003e rwa status -\u003e landmark -\u003e digest -\u003e\n   journal delta). Lesson BODIES are drill-down on trigger, not bulk-loaded;\n   turn.md is the one file that loads whole, because it annotates every\n   digest the loop reads.\n\n2. \"Morning checklist at each in-game day start\" is reshaped: turn.md\n   trip-wires apply to EVERY digest (zero extra queries — thresholds over\n   fields already in hand); triggered.md fires on the loop's own acts and on\n   journal events (its colony-start section is the staged-fixture sequence);\n   daily.md runs at the first read after digest.time.day_of_season changes.\n   The reshape exists because the loop's rhythm, not the player's, is the\n   unit — the argument is in checklists/README.md.\n\n3. The artifact your verification's Addition 2 asked for is defined:\n   append one NDJSON line per evaluation to RUNS/\u003crun\u003e/checklist.ndjson —\n   {\"day\",\"tick\",\"item\",\"verdict\":\"ok|action|blocked|n/a\",\"reading\",\"note\"}.\n   A silent skip is a missing line, which makes your \"no silent skips\"\n   invariant a diff instead of a judgement. blocked names the issue id it\n   waits on (3.3/3.6 items log blocked today rather than vanishing). Same\n   file feeds 4.4's retirement ledger; commented there too.\n\n4. Two loop obligations 4.1 deliberately did NOT absorb, so they are not\n   double-specified: dialog-halt termination (your verification's Addition 1)\n   and undraft discipline stay in this spec's skill text. The checklists\n   reference undraft only inside the raid-end trigger's interim procedure,\n   which retires wholesale into cc8988c's mod procedure when that ships.","files":null}]}